NAME
    usb-install.sh - flash verified boot-only m-boot image and provision ext4

SYNOPSIS
    ./usb-install.sh

DESCRIPTION
    Operator-controlled destructive installer for Linux x86_64 and ARM64.
    No whole-disk device is accepted as a CLI operand or chosen by default.
    The command lists actual physical disks, displays their identity and
    layout, and requires the user to type ERASE followed by the exact
    chosen device identifier. It refuses system mountpoints, active swap,
    unstable disk identity and unsupported logical-sector sizes.

    After confirmation it streams the SHA256-verified 576 MiB boot-only
    image onto the selected whole disk, reads back the written region
    and verifies its hash BEFORE modifying GPT. It relocates the backup
    GPT to the actual end of the device, verifies BIOS/ESP partition
    geometry and the absence of partition 3, and only then creates
    partition 3 (Linux GPT type 8300) using the remaining usable space.
    Formats partition 3 ext4 as MBOOTDATA, assigns the invoking user
    ownership of the ext4 root, creates /m/boot/iso and checks the
    filesystem. No GRUB build is done on the installer host.

BOOT-ONLY IMAGE GEOMETRY (512-byte logical sectors)
    Published raw image: 603979776 bytes (576 MiB).
    Partition 1: EF02, LBAs 2048..22527 (10 MiB BIOS Boot)
    Partition 2: EF00, LBAs 22528..1071103 (512 MiB FAT32 ESP)
    Partition 3: ABSENT, created by installer only.
    Backup GPT: at the end of the 576 MiB distributed raw image.

    The resulting installed disk has the same firmware partitions
    plus ext4 MBOOTDATA starting at LBA 1071104, ending at the last
    usable sector before the relocated backup GPT. GPT disk and
    partition IDs are regenerated so cloned media do not share IDs.

PROVENANCE AND INTEGRITY
    images/m-boot-combined.raw.gz, m-boot-loader.zip,
    SHA256SUMS, RAW-SHA256SUMS and BUILD-INFO.txt are committed to Git
    by the x86_64 build workflow. BUILD-INFO must explicitly declare
    partition_count=2 and image_bytes=603979776. Older images (including
    the original 2 GiB images containing partition 3) are rejected
    BEFORE any destructive write. GRUB firmware and m-loader resources
    live exclusively on the FAT32 ESP. Data ISO payloads are not baked
    into the published image.

REQUIREMENTS AND SCOPE
    Linux x86_64/ARM64, POSIX sh, gzip, unzip, sha256sum, dd,
    util-linux block tools, gdisk/sgdisk, e2fsprogs, mount/umount
    and administrator authentication. Only 512-byte logical-sector
    physical disks of at least 2 GiB are supported in this release.
    The operating-system source filesystem is not modified.

    This installer is deliberately NOT a migration or update command:
    it erases ALL partitions and files on the selected whole disk.
    The operator alone owns backing up and restoring old USB files,
    and decides separately when to authorize real physical flashing.
    macOS native ext4 mounting and Windows boot are not current goals.

VALIDATION
    Verify SHA256, compact GPT with exactly two partitions, staged
    firmware/ESP modules, and a disposable larger-disk provisioning
    trial before physical flashing. QEMU BIOS, x86_64 UEFI and ARM64 UEFI
    firmware tests require their own observed results. Reaching the
    Ubuntu installer transition then running out of QEMU RAM is NOT
    a complete Ubuntu boot PASS.

